  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on identifying the most probable outcome of each lottery and then comparing their favorability (likely in value), preferring the one with the more favorable (higher-value) most probable outcome. In this case, that would be Lottery A (6000 Euros at 45% vs. 3000 Euros at 90%). However, the individual chose B based on the high probability (90%) of winning, not because 3000 Euros is a more favorable outcome than 6000 Euros. In fact, the individual’s reasoning emphasizes probability of winning, not the value of the most likely outcome. Therefore, the information considered (high chance of winning) and the justification (safety/sureness) do not align with the decision reason, which would point toward A if applied consistently. The individual did not use the rule of comparing the favorability of the most probable outcomes; instead, they used a probability-maximizing or risk-aversion heuristic. The mismatch in both information considered and decision rule leads to the conclusion that the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
}

